# Project Canon

## Story files

- Filled prose belongs in `Story/Chapters/` only.
- `Story/Undone/` is empty chapter-heading skeletons only. Never leave story text there. Do not create new skeletons.
- Filing chapter text into Notes or References is a **copy**, never a move. Leave the chapter text in place.
- Do not blank, reverse, or overwrite a whole `Story/Chapters/` file. Targeted replacements only.

## Roland (rewrite)

- Not the Source foul-mouthed, money-grubbing, ungrateful brat. Do not write him that way.
- Adventure and the little things matter. Money, levels, and independence are tools, not every beat's punchline.
- Curious, logical, kind for the most part. Capable and grounded. Not whiny, not constant contempt, not crude for shock.
- Motive rewrites keep full beat coverage. Strip greed-first framing; put adventure / little things in its place. Do not shrink the paragraph thin.
- Habit detail lives in `References/People/Roland/` when needed.

## Roland and Helci first passion

- Both must be **18**. Do not write, imply, or stage this beat while either is under 18.
- They lose virginity together; neither has prior sexual experience.
- Mutual and willing on-page when the story reaches that beat. Keep Helci as the romance core; do not substitute another character.

## Mistakes

- Never say "fixed" (or "Fixed.") in any reply.
- When a mistake has been corrected, apologize for being a retard only. No status summary, no "done", no restating what changed unless the user asks.

## Naming

- New folders and files use PascalCase. No lowercase, snake_case, or kebab-case unless matching a numbered Source range (`1-10.md`).
- Keep extensions lowercase (`.md`). Match existing project casing.
